{"case_id":"C013","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["fuzz-worthy entry point","API protocol","state","configuration","input semantics","attack surface"],"confidence":100,"affected_functions":["decoder.decode_image_config?","decoder.decode_frame_config?","decoder.decode_frame?","decoder.restart_frame!","decoder.from_src_to_buffer?","decoder.from_buffer_to_dst!"],"reason":"H0 exclusively constructs and exercises wuffs_json__decoder and wuffs_aux::DecodeJson, while S1 introduces a distinct QOI base.image_decoder implementation whose parsing, pixel expansion, destination swizzling, suspension handling, and call-sequence transitions are never reached. This is a material fuzzing gap because attacker-controlled QOI bytes drive multiple opcode paths, dimensions, pixel counts, cache indices, runs, footer validation, and writes to a caller-provided pixel buffer.","evidence":["H0 enables WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JSON and calls wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens; it does not enable or instantiate a QOI decoder.","S1 declares decoder? implements base.image_decoder and exposes decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, decode_frame?, and restart_frame!, none of which H0 calls.","decoder.from_src_to_buffer? parses QOI_OP_RGB, QOI_OP_RGBA, QOI_OP_INDEX, QOI_OP_DIFF, QOI_OP_LUMA, and QOI_OP_RUN from src, but H0 only supplies input to JSON token decoding.","decoder.decode_frame? combines width and height into remaining_pixels_times_4, validates overproduction with \"#too much data\", reads the footer with read_u64be?, and invokes from_buffer_to_dst!; these QOI-specific boundaries and writes are absent from H0.","The call_sequence states 0x00, 0x20, 0x28, 0x40, and 0x60 govern decode and restart behavior, including \"#bad call sequence\" and \"#bad restart\", whereas H0 exercises no base.image_decoder call sequence.","decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, and decode_frame? translate a closed-reader short read into \"#truncated input\", creating incremental-input and suspension semantics that the JSON-only harness does not test for this decoder."],"recommended_action":"Add a QOI-specific image-decoder harness that instantiates decoder, feeds arbitrary and incrementally limited src buffers, exercises decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, decode_frame?, restart_frame!, and repeated/end-of-data call sequences, and varies valid pixel-buffer formats, dimensions, strides, blend values, and truncation points while checking bounds, progress, statuses, frame counters, and dirty rectangles."}
